1
00:00:11,845 --> 00:00:14,597
{\an8}Okay! Remember,
this regatta is a head race.

2
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:17,434
It's 6K, long haul, not a sprint.

3
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:19,769
Doing well at the Head of the Laurence
is a barometer

4
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:21,271
for how the rest of the season goes.

5
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:24,315
Including the Haverford Cup. Okay?

6
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:26,484
Okay, come on, Eagles, let's go!

7
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:32,073
Picking up the pace
in five, six, seven, eight.

8
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,825
["Freak It" by Kim Petras playing]

9
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:36,411
-[heavy EDM beat thumping]
-[rowers grunting]

10
00:00:36,494 --> 00:00:38,580
-[Ryder] Can you go faster?
-[Josh] Faster than you!

11
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:39,497
[Ryder] Watch me.

12
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:41,291
[Josh] We got this.

13
00:00:44,627 --> 00:00:46,755
[Teagan] Feel the beat,
you guys! Keep going.

14
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:51,051
Whoo! Let's go! Come on!

15
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:52,677
[Josh] Come on, Quaid!

16
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:55,346
[Teagan] Let's go, guys!

17
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:59,309
-[Quaid] Yeah!
-[team exclaiming]

18
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,854
[Hayden] EDM this early in the morning?

19
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:05,398
How is this helping the boat?

20
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:08,943
You said it's my job to run conditioning.
You didn't say how.

21
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:11,029
[Crabcatcher] Out of my way!

22
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:15,075
[vomiting]

23
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:16,785
And we're done.

24
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:27,712
Would you look at that?

25
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:31,091
We might have a fighting chance
at top five at the Head of the Laurence.

26
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:34,552
{\an8}-And look at you.
-I hit a new personal best lately.

27
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:37,722
{\an8}-I gotta keep up with the boys.
-Are you ready for this weekend?

28
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,724
{\an8}'Cause head races are coxswain races.

29
00:01:39,808 --> 00:01:44,938
{\an8}All those twists and turns on the course…
The boat lives and dies by your steering.

30
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:48,525
All good.
I'm practicing on <i>Mario Kart</i>. [laughs]

31
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:51,736
Yeah, I've been mapping out the course.

32
00:01:52,237 --> 00:01:53,696
-I'll be ready.
-Okay.

33
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:55,990
All right, boys.

34
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:58,910
This is it.
First away regatta of the season.

35
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:00,120
-We will be packing up…
-Whoo!

36
00:02:00,203 --> 00:02:01,621
…at the boathouse at 8 a.m.

37
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:05,125
…and hitting the road at 9.
Now hit the showers.

38
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:07,085
-Okay.
-All right.

39
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,545
-Coming, Crabby?
-Up you get.

40
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:09,504
-Come on!
-Stop!

41
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:12,882
I never thought I'd see the day these boys
would work out to your playlist.

42
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:13,800
[laughs]

43
00:02:13,883 --> 00:02:16,553
You brought them together.
Good job, Coxie.

44
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:19,097
[rower] All right.

45
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:21,808
[clears throat]

46
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:24,477
-Dude, put me down!
-No!

47
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:32,110
Teagan. There's something
I want to talk to you about.

48
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:34,279
Uh, yeah. What's up?

49
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:36,489
What are you doing
after the regatta next week?

50
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:40,368
Uh, other than practice, nothing.

51
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:43,746
Hey, Teagan. Here's your charger.
Thanks for letting me borrow it.

52
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:45,456
No problem.

53
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:48,751
[Josh] You need help
tidying up or anything?

54
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:50,545
[intriguing music playing]

55
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:52,755
Josh, I think I saw
your girlfriend outside.

56
00:02:58,011 --> 00:03:00,346
All right. Uh, I'll catch you later?

57
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,431
Yeah.

58
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:02,432
Cool.

59
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:09,063
Hey, where were we?

60
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:11,399
Dude, what's up with Josh?
He's getting friendly.

61
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:14,819
He's just being nice, and…

62
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:17,530
you know, he's really not that bad.

63
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:21,993
-Are we talking about the same guy?
-You could give him a chance.

64
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:25,121
Okay. You guys are acting different.

65
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:28,082
Is there something going on with you two?

66
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,542
[laughs awkwardly]

67
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:35,798
Yeah, I think
you're more interested in Josh than me.

68
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:43,681
What?

69
00:03:44,974 --> 00:03:47,227
-That should be the last box.
-Wow.

70
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,229
You said that three boxes ago.

71
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:52,106
The Crab Shack has to get extra
when it's chowder week.

72
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:53,399
-Chowder week?
-Yeah.

73
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:55,526
It's in all the guidebooks.

74
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:59,447
They come for our fall colors.
They stay for our fishy stew.

75
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:00,490
Ew.

76
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:01,658
[both laughing]

77
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:03,076
It is kind of gross.

78
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:04,911
I'll settle up with Fran.
Meet you at the car.

79
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:05,954
Sounds good.

80
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:09,999
[man] I need more ice. More ice.

81
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,459
Who is he?

82
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:13,544
Matt? He's an old friend of mine.

83
00:04:13,628 --> 00:04:16,631
Jim put his back out,
so he's giving me a helping hand.

84
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:18,091
Nice hands.

85
00:04:18,174 --> 00:04:22,387
-The rest of him is even nicer.
-Oh, my goodness, Fran!

86
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:23,346
I am married.

87
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:26,224
Didn't stop your husband
from running out on you and your girl.

88
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,893
Uh, well…

89
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,271
A bit more complicated than that, but--

90
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:35,024
All I know is that man just carried
90 lbs of fish for you. With a smile.

91
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:37,193
Keep holding on to something complicated,

92
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:40,822
you'll miss something
that makes a whole lot more sense.

93
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:45,702
Thanks.

94
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:49,163
[lively music, party chatter]

95
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,542
[laughing]

96
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:54,043
She can't do that.

97
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:55,503
I mean, let's…

98
00:04:55,586 --> 00:04:57,422
-[Josh] There they are.
-[Ryder] There they are.

99
00:04:57,922 --> 00:04:59,090
[Josh] Hey.

100
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,259
[Ryder] You look beautiful tonight.

101
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:02,427
Thank you for noticing.

102
00:05:03,928 --> 00:05:05,888
Water's up!

103
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:08,433
-Pasta incoming!
-[Teagan] Go! Go.

104
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:09,517
[Noah] I'm starving.

105
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:12,270
[Teagan clears throat] Thank you.

106
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:15,440
Why am I being assaulted by sad linguini?

107
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:18,026
It's a crew tradition.
We carb load before the regatta.

108
00:05:18,109 --> 00:05:19,694
Just follow my lead, okay?

109
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:22,572
All right! Everybody got their pasghetti?

110
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:23,614
[all assenting]

111
00:05:23,698 --> 00:05:25,283
[Baloo] Three, two, one…

112
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:27,368
[all] Free speed!

113
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,662
[Britney] Don't get pasta water on me!

114
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:31,873
[Teagan] Free speed is
a rowing superstition.

115
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:33,583
It's our ritual that brings us good luck.

116
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:35,835
It might help give us
a little extra boost.

117
00:05:35,918 --> 00:05:37,754
-Yeah.
-You need a sacrifice.

118
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:39,464
Perry's outfit will do the trick.

119
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:42,508
-Get some?
-I need all the extra speed I can get.

120
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:45,428
Hey, don't worry. You've got this.

121
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:47,347
I barfed at practice.

122
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:49,557
But only once this time.

123
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:50,808
[groans]

124
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:52,560
-Hey.
-I keep having that nightmare

125
00:05:52,643 --> 00:05:56,230
where my arms give out during the race,
and I don't think I can keep up.

126
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:58,775
Maybe you could, like,
steer the boat into a bridge

127
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:00,651
so I won't be the reason we all lose?

128
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:02,528
You are not going to fail.

129
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:05,865
We've been working on your conditioning
for weeks. Come on!

130
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:07,617
Crabby.

131
00:06:08,242 --> 00:06:10,370
I believe in you, and I've got your back.

132
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:13,790
Look, I was gonna jog
part of the course before the race.

133
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:16,167
Thought I'd map it out. You wanna come?

134
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:19,128
You'll see, it's not as long as you think.
Plus, extra cardio.

135
00:06:19,212 --> 00:06:20,880
Okay, yeah, sounds good.

136
00:06:20,963 --> 00:06:23,966
-Extra cardio. No, thanks.
-Yeah, of course not.

137
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:25,968
Extra cardio is
just for the rest of us mortals.

138
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:28,429
Yeah, I mean,
you just show up, row, and go home.

139
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:30,515
-You don't even gotta think about it.
-[laughing]

140
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:33,434
I mean, I… I think about it.

141
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:36,521
All right, listen up!
Your stroke is talking.

142
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:44,028
This is the year
that we knock West Fail off the podium.

143
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:44,987
You with me?

144
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:47,698
[all cheering and agreeing]

145
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:50,660
He's really putting on a show tonight.

146
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:53,121
Girl, you're drooling.
Do you need a bib, or are you good?

147
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:57,125
[all chanting]
<i>Easton, Easton, our home on high</i>

148
00:06:57,208 --> 00:07:00,878
<i>Lifting, soaring to the sky</i>

149
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:07,343
<i>Spread our wings with talons bright</i>
<i>Enemies running from the sight</i>

150
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:13,683
<i>A mighty eagle, king of birds</i>
<i>Watch your butt 'cause you've been served</i>

151
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:17,895
[all cheering and applauding]

152
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:20,690
Eagle pride! Eagle pride!

153
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:25,528
Okay. Let's be real,
it's an improvement on the design.

154
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:28,030
<i>It's not about the swag,</i>
<i>but the man underneath.</i>

155
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:30,408
<i>I think you should try it out. Put it on.</i>

156
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:36,205
[laughs] Okay.

157
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:54,182
<i>Who's a bad little fanboy?</i>

158
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:55,683
[laughing]

159
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:57,935
-This is kind of working.
-What are you doing?

160
00:07:58,519 --> 00:07:59,729
Gotta go.

161
00:07:59,812 --> 00:08:01,772
You saw nothing.

162
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:04,817
Tell me you're not hooking up
with some loser from Westvale.

163
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,736
West Fail's the enemy.

164
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,488
I know. That's what makes it so hot.

165
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:10,114
Are you insane?

166
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:12,366
The team's gonna lose their minds
if they find out.

167
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:14,494
-You have to break up with him.
-Hear me out.

168
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:16,412
What if I don't?

169
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:19,332
[mischievous music playing]

170
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:22,376
-What are you doing?
-Interesting. No, I'm not doing anything.

171
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,879
Dump him. Do it.

172
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:26,631
Don't make me use this.

173
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:35,223
First a stain on my dress and now this!

174
00:08:40,228 --> 00:08:41,521
-Hey.
-Hi.

175
00:08:41,604 --> 00:08:43,272
Dress okay?

176
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:48,027
Uh, it's… It's gonna be
a replacement situation.

177
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:50,780
[laughs] You know, dresses.
They're kinda like boyfriends.

178
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:56,744
So, you are still mad at me.

179
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:58,621
Yeah.

180
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:01,290
Look… I'm sorry.

181
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:03,334
I ditched you.

182
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,254
Okay? But the after party wasn't planned.

183
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:08,297
-It just happened.
-With the whole crew.

184
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:12,552
And somehow they got the memo.
Even Teagan got an invite.

185
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:19,976
You have every right to be mad.

186
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:22,395
But it was an accident.

187
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,480
What's been going on with you?

188
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,151
Be real with me.

189
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:34,115
Sometimes, I wonder what would happen
if my life just blew up.

190
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:36,117
-Your life isn't gonna blow up.
-What if it did?

191
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:39,161
Would it be so bad
to figure out something new?

192
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:40,830
Being someone other than a Regis.

193
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:42,873
That's ridiculous. Babe…

194
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:48,045
Don't let your family competition
get in your head. You are gonna win.

195
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:50,590
You know I only pick winners.

196
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,719
Yeah, I thought you'd say that.

197
00:09:54,802 --> 00:09:55,803
Yeah.

198
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:59,682
I'll, uh, get you a drink.

199
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:01,100
Okay.

200
00:10:12,695 --> 00:10:14,822
-[Britney] Hm.
-Trouble in paradise?

201
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:17,908
Nothing that can't be fixed.

202
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:20,119
So, what are you going to do?

203
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:23,372
-Do you have a plan?
-I always have a plan.

204
00:10:23,956 --> 00:10:28,127
Keep your friends close,
and your enemies even closer.

205
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:31,839
-And keep your best friends even closer?
-Hey, Teagan.

206
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:33,215
-Hi.
-Hi.

207
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:34,800
-Hi.
-Hi.

208
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:37,428
I'm staying at the same hotel
at the regatta,

209
00:10:37,511 --> 00:10:38,929
and I was wondering

210
00:10:39,013 --> 00:10:42,183
if you wanted to do a girls' night?
Nails, facials, that kind of thing?

211
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,393
Just the two of us?

212
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:47,688
Look, I know that
we got off to a rough start.

213
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:51,901
But we're a part of the same world now.
It's time to start over.

214
00:10:52,401 --> 00:10:53,402
Yes?

215
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:56,364
Uh, okay. Yeah, sure.

216
00:10:56,447 --> 00:10:58,199
-Why not?
-Great.

217
00:10:58,282 --> 00:10:59,492
-[laughs]
-[Teagan] Yeah.

218
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:01,077
Great.

219
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:06,415
[girl] Is that her?

220
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:08,668
Who?

221
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:10,294
The girl you've been crushing on?

222
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:11,379
Madison.

223
00:11:11,462 --> 00:11:15,341
I may not go to your chichi prep school,
but I've known you since you were 10.

224
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:17,385
That face says you're crushing.

225
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:21,305
-Must Coach Hayden bring you everywhere?
-[Madison] Daughter privileges.

226
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,057
You should ask her out.

227
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:25,768
I did.

228
00:11:25,851 --> 00:11:27,269
Really? Did she say yes?

229
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:30,356
She said, "I think
you're more interested in Josh than me."

230
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:32,149
Going out on a limb here…

231
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:33,484
You did it wrong.

232
00:11:33,567 --> 00:11:36,904
-[Cam] Tell me something I don't know.
-Walk me through the crime scene.

233
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:38,155
I came in.

234
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:40,658
I was just about to ask her out,
and then Josh interrupted.

235
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:43,119
-And he was being his usual Josh self.
-Stop.

236
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:45,246
There's already
way too much Josh in this story.

237
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:46,205
What happened next?

238
00:11:46,288 --> 00:11:48,833
There was a vibe. I asked
if something was going on between them.

239
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:50,334
Oh my God.

240
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:51,919
Maybe that was very wrong.

241
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:53,087
You think?

242
00:11:54,088 --> 00:11:56,716
-You need to apologize to her, like, now.
-About the Josh thing?

243
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:59,719
-No! Do not mention Josh.
-Okay.

244
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,512
-Okay?
-Okay, yeah.

245
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:03,431
["Run Free" by Soulwax playing]

246
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:05,266
<i>♪ Beautiful mistake ♪</i>

247
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:08,519
<i>♪ Try not to lose it ♪</i>

248
00:12:11,772 --> 00:12:13,774
<i>♪ I wanna run free ♪</i>

249
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:16,902
<i>♪ With the music ♪</i>

250
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:20,197
-Thank you. Okay, can you hold my stuff?
-Huh?

251
00:12:20,281 --> 00:12:22,867
I wanna check out the Jacuzzi.
See if it's a good one or scuzzy one.

252
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:23,909
Wha…

253
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:24,952
Thank you.

254
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:26,412
[sighs]

255
00:12:27,705 --> 00:12:29,290
Hi. I have a reservation.

256
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:30,374
Wonderful.

257
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:33,169
Happy anniversary, Mrs. Tao.

258
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:35,129
You and your husband
are platinum-level guests,

259
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:37,423
which makes you eligible
for a free upgrade.

260
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:40,968
I'm sorry, I totally forgot.

261
00:12:41,051 --> 00:12:43,179
It's fine. I did too.

262
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:48,058
-Actually, my husband and I are not…
-You know what? We'll take the upgrade.

263
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:49,560
-Thanks.
-[Ella laughs]

264
00:12:50,686 --> 00:12:51,687
The least Dad could do.

265
00:12:51,771 --> 00:12:53,439
[Baloo] I know we can win again.

266
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:56,525
Hey, I have a fun idea. Why don't we
order room service tomorrow night?

267
00:12:56,609 --> 00:13:00,279
It won't be an anniversary dinner,
but… it'll be a "you and me" hang.

268
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:02,281
-I'll order steak.
-I'll order a cake.

269
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:04,700
-Steak and cake it is.
-Here are your keys, Mrs. Tao.

270
00:13:04,784 --> 00:13:05,785
Thank you.

271
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:07,286
Thanks.

272
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,501
[clears throat]

273
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:20,257
You're taller in person.

274
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:21,342
You're not.

275
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:24,261
We said we wouldn't talk here.

276
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,890
I know. I just, uh…

277
00:13:29,558 --> 00:13:30,726
wanted to say hi.

278
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:34,146
I gotta get back to my team.

279
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,105
You mean your cult?

280
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:36,941
That cult's beat Easton ten years running.

281
00:13:37,024 --> 00:13:39,652
I'd say bring your A game,
but who are we kidding?

282
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:41,904
Easton barely has C- game.

283
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:42,905
[snickers]

284
00:13:42,988 --> 00:13:45,324
Run your mouth.
It's the only thing fast about you.

285
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:52,706
Yeah, we really shouldn't talk here.

286
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:54,542
Yeah.

287
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:57,253
See you around.

288
00:13:58,045 --> 00:13:59,046
Yeah.

289
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:16,438
Oh, hey!

290
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:17,523
Hey.

291
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,150
Why are you jogging in the stairwell?

292
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:22,570
Getting in extra conditioning.

293
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:26,323
You know, fighting my way back to stroke.
Where are you headed?

294
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:27,992
-I have a date…
-Really?

295
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:29,368
With your girlfriend.

296
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:31,996
Oh, that's, um… weird.

297
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:33,998
Is that weird?

298
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:37,001
Well, you two
don't really like each other.

299
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:40,921
And aren't things, like,
a little different with…

300
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:43,632
Is something different?

301
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,552
You know what? Of course not.

302
00:14:47,803 --> 00:14:49,555
-Have a good time.
-Thank you.

303
00:14:52,474 --> 00:14:53,309
[knocking]

304
00:14:53,392 --> 00:14:54,602
[Britney] Come in.

305
00:14:57,479 --> 00:14:58,522
Wow.

306
00:14:58,606 --> 00:14:59,857
Sit!

307
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,191
-Okay. Yeah.
-Please.

308
00:15:03,611 --> 00:15:04,612
Tea?

309
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:06,906
Oh, wow.

310
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:08,824
So…

311
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:13,203
Girl talk.
I see that you're cozying up to the team.

312
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:14,788
Any sparks flying?

313
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:17,082
Uh… Sparks?

314
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:20,753
Don't tell me you spend
all your mornings and evenings

315
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:22,504
with eight hotties and feel nothing.

316
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:24,256
We mostly talk about rowing.

317
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:29,720
-Have you ever thought about Quaid?
-He's like a little brother.

318
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:31,263
Hm. Noah?

319
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:34,600
-He's like an older brother.
-What about Cam?

320
00:15:34,683 --> 00:15:37,937
He's cute. Don't tell me
you wouldn't drink that eight pack.

321
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,648
He's very… drinkable.

322
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:41,941
[laughs uncomfortably]

323
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:47,029
Have you ever thought about Josh?

324
00:15:47,529 --> 00:15:49,531
[tense music playing]

325
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:52,868
Okay.

326
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:57,414
Britney, why am I really here?

327
00:15:58,666 --> 00:15:59,667
[sighs]

328
00:16:00,292 --> 00:16:03,462
Cards on the table. I want you gone.

329
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:09,301
Okay, wow. Cards on the table,
I'm not going anywhere.

330
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:11,178
You sure about that?

331
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:24,650
You feeding the fish?

332
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:28,654
It's a very important team tradition
done independently of the team.

333
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:31,031
Well, don't play coy with me.

334
00:16:31,115 --> 00:16:32,408
[both laugh]

335
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:35,077
-You proud of that one?
-Just a little bit.

336
00:16:36,578 --> 00:16:37,746
Can you give me some?

337
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:47,923
Are you always this quiet
when nobody's looking?

338
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:51,844
Depends on who's looking.

339
00:17:02,312 --> 00:17:03,439
Say "when."

340
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:06,025
When.

341
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:11,989
[dreamy music playing]

342
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:23,000
[indistinct chatter in distance]

343
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:25,836
-Come on.
-[Perry] You know how that worked out.

344
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:28,338
I was looking at your socials.

345
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:32,801
You're the Southwest junior champion
in single sculls. I bet you miss rowing.

346
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:35,304
Yeah, I do.

347
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:36,680
So?

348
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:39,725
So did you know
that the best school for girls' crew

349
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:41,268
is Gravenhurst Academy?

350
00:17:41,977 --> 00:17:43,812
I know you do because you follow them.

351
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:47,733
Yeah, they're the best crew
on the East Coast.

352
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:49,234
So what if you could go there?

353
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:52,988
My mom went to Gravenhurst,
as an equestrian, of course.

354
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,032
Now she's friends with the head of school.

355
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:58,035
I can make a call right now
and get you a tryout for tomorrow morning.

356
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:00,037
If you want it.

357
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:03,207
Are you serious?

358
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:04,166
Yes.

359
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:13,383
But if I got in,
I'd have to leave the guys.

360
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:14,885
That's the point.

361
00:18:14,968 --> 00:18:17,262
But you get rowing back.

362
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:22,017
It's a win-win, babe.
If this works, you get what you want.

363
00:18:24,103 --> 00:18:25,104
Yeah.

364
00:18:27,314 --> 00:18:28,732
Make the call.

365
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:35,155
[Noah] Dude, hold on. Did…

366
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:37,533
Did Baloo even text you back
about training yet?

367
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:40,702
No. Radio silence.
Guess he doesn't think he needs to train.

368
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:43,705
[Noah] Bare necessities?
More like bare minimum.

369
00:18:43,789 --> 00:18:45,374
[Perry] I mean, to be fair,

370
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:48,210
dude can roll right out of bed
and into the boat and be good to go.

371
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:49,878
-[melancholy music playing]
-[scoffs]

372
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:51,839
Are you okay?

373
00:18:53,715 --> 00:18:54,758
They think I don't try.

374
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:57,970
-Why does everybody always think that?
-Everybody?

375
00:18:58,053 --> 00:19:03,600
The team, teachers… my mom, my sister.

376
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:06,353
I do try.

377
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:09,022
I guess you make things look easy.

378
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:16,363
Hey, look, it sucks when people
don't notice how hard you're working.

379
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,782
It makes you feel taken for granted.

380
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:20,075
Yeah.

381
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:22,411
Another way of looking at it…

382
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:26,081
You're reliable.
They know they can count on you.

383
00:19:26,957 --> 00:19:28,625
-Reliable?
-[laughs]

384
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:30,252
It's not exactly a sexy reputation.

385
00:19:30,335 --> 00:19:32,462
Well, they don't have to find you sexy.

386
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:33,881
Just me.

387
00:19:42,014 --> 00:19:44,224
You are hilarious.

388
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:48,270
Well, I guess I'll see you later.

389
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,732
-Oh! Hey.
-Hey.

390
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:55,360
-Should have gone for it. [laughs]
-Yeah, no, that was not happening.

391
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:56,737
Can't hook up at a regatta.

392
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:58,322
-What?
-It's always another coach.

393
00:19:58,405 --> 00:20:01,325
Or in this case… someone's parent.

394
00:20:01,408 --> 00:20:04,119
Oh… I can see why that would be awkward.

395
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:05,996
-Mm-hmm.
-[laughs awkwardly]

396
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:09,082
Is it hard… dating again?

397
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:13,253
Dating now is kind of a blood sport.
And it's harder when you have a kid.

398
00:20:13,337 --> 00:20:14,588
Does Madison know you date?

399
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:16,381
Tell you what,
it's better when she doesn't.

400
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:19,218
But somehow she always knows.

401
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:20,928
[Ella sighs]

402
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:24,223
Do you think about getting back out there?

403
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:25,974
Um, I'm starting to.

404
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:29,937
What even is there in Eagle's Cove?

405
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:32,773
You know, the rep cinema's
playing <i>Roman Holiday</i>.

406
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:34,149
[Ella gasps]

407
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:36,526
I love that movie.

408
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,237
I know you do.

409
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:39,738
We could go.

410
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:44,493
-I'm just… I'm not…
-I know, you're not ready.

411
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:48,038
Sorry. I ruined it.

412
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:52,834
There's nothing to apologize for.
It takes longer to let go than you expect.

413
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,336
And that's okay.

414
00:20:57,881 --> 00:21:01,760
All right, well,
I guess I'm gonna… turn in early.

415
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:02,844
Okay.

416
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:05,222
Take care, El.

417
00:21:06,556 --> 00:21:09,017
[bittersweet music playing]

418
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:16,066
[elevator bell dings]

419
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:20,070
-Hey.
-Ah, hi.

420
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:22,864
How was girls' night?

421
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,908
Total blast.

422
00:21:25,575 --> 00:21:27,995
Did you talk about boys?

423
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:30,455
Yeah. She thinks
something's up with you and me.

424
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:33,583
And she wants me
as far away from you as possible.

425
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:35,877
-I mean, it's ridiculous.
-Is it?

426
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:42,426
-What are you talking about?
-Teagan, what are we doing here?

427
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:45,012
Are you telling me you don't think about
the night at the docks?

428
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,018
-Shit. This is a problem.
-Oh…

429
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:53,228
You're telling me. I have a girlfriend.

430
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:56,398
-And I maybe have something with Cam.
-You do?

431
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:59,359
-These are not good feelings.
-Well deduced, Sherlock.

432
00:21:59,443 --> 00:22:00,944
She's literally messaging me right now.

433
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:03,280
Don't answer. I don't wanna
go behind my girlfriend's back.

434
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:05,866
-Neither do I. That girl's terrifying.
-Just friends?

435
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:07,200
Friends.

436
00:22:10,829 --> 00:22:11,830
Okay.

437
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:14,166
[exhales]

438
00:22:22,382 --> 00:22:24,551
[Britney] <i>Hey, girl. Got your tryout.</i>

439
00:22:24,634 --> 00:22:28,638
<i>Meet Gravenhurst at the erg room</i>
<i>at 6:30. Good luck. B.</i>

440
00:22:28,722 --> 00:22:30,015
[Teagan groans]

441
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:33,935
What… in the…

442
00:22:34,019 --> 00:22:35,771
[Ella laughs]

443
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:37,481
What's this about?

444
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:43,362
I was invited to erg with a school
with an elite rowing program.

445
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:46,323
I don't know what any of those words mean.

446
00:22:46,406 --> 00:22:49,201
-Sorry.
-It's code for tryout.

447
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,578
Well, why so sneaky?

448
00:22:52,329 --> 00:22:53,288
I don't want a poach,

449
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:56,375
and I don't want the guys to find out
I'm talking to other teams.

450
00:22:57,334 --> 00:23:00,504
Just, they'd be hurt if they knew
I was thinking of leaving them.

451
00:23:01,338 --> 00:23:05,550
Oh, well, it's just a tryout.
You could bomb.

452
00:23:05,634 --> 00:23:07,552
-Mom!
-[laughing]

453
00:23:09,179 --> 00:23:10,430
Break an arm, babe.

454
00:23:11,098 --> 00:23:11,932
[Teagan laughs]

455
00:23:12,015 --> 00:23:14,643
Will you just get off my leg?
It's cramping.

456
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:17,854
[upbeat music playing]

457
00:23:21,858 --> 00:23:25,237
-Hey, there's Teagan. Go talk to her.
-It's 6:30 a.m.

458
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:27,239
-It's not a good time.
-Not a request. Go.

459
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:28,490
Now.

460
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,576
Hey. Morning.

461
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:33,370
-Uh, hey.
-Where are you headed?

462
00:23:33,453 --> 00:23:36,998
Nowhere special. I'm just…
I'm meeting my mom.

463
00:23:37,082 --> 00:23:39,960
I just wanted to apologize
about the Josh thing.

464
00:23:40,043 --> 00:23:42,254
I don't wanna talk about Josh.
Enough about him.

465
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:44,172
That's not what I wanna talk about.

466
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:48,927
I was wondering if… you wanted
to hang out with me sometime.

467
00:23:49,010 --> 00:23:50,137
[romantic music playing]

468
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:53,014
Yes, I do. I'd love to.

469
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:55,350
Um, there's this new
Mexican food truck in town.

470
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:58,019
Tacos are my love language.

471
00:23:59,229 --> 00:24:01,690
-Can we talk about this later?
-Sure.

472
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:03,692
[music distorts to a stop]

473
00:24:06,278 --> 00:24:07,154
What?

474
00:24:07,654 --> 00:24:09,614
Oof. I'm sorry that didn't work out.

475
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:10,657
She said yes.

476
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:11,783
-She did?
-Yeah.

477
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:13,577
Well, I really read that wrong.

478
00:24:15,162 --> 00:24:16,496
Hi!

479
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:19,833
Thank you so much for meeting with me.
I really appreciate it.

480
00:24:19,916 --> 00:24:21,626
Well, it's a favor to the principal.

481
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:23,420
Ah. Got it.

482
00:24:23,503 --> 00:24:27,048
So, you won gold last year in the single,
but now you're coxing an eight?

483
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:30,969
Yes, but I keep my erg training up.
The single is my passion.

484
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:35,307
Then let's talk times. For the 2K,
our U-17 girls hit 7:40, sometimes faster.

485
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:37,309
Great. Me too.

486
00:24:37,851 --> 00:24:40,145
-Okay, then. Let's go.
-Okay.

487
00:24:40,228 --> 00:24:41,688
[clears throat]

488
00:24:41,771 --> 00:24:43,899
["Accelerator" by Blusher playing]

489
00:24:43,982 --> 00:24:46,943
{\an8}<i>-♪ Sometimes I feel like a wanna jump… ♪</i>
-[stopwatch beeps]

490
00:24:47,527 --> 00:24:48,528
Come on.

491
00:24:49,279 --> 00:24:51,323
<i>♪ When I'm looking at you ♪</i>

492
00:24:51,948 --> 00:24:56,786
<i>♪ Sometimes I feel like I wanna</i>
<i>Push down the accelerator ♪</i>

493
00:24:56,870 --> 00:24:59,164
<i>♪ When I'm looking at you ♪</i>

494
00:24:59,247 --> 00:25:04,628
<i>♪ Sometimes I feel like I wanna</i>
<i>Push down the accelerator ♪</i>

495
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:10,342
-[stopwatch beeps]
-Stop.

496
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:14,554
7:32.

497
00:25:15,138 --> 00:25:16,139
Darn.

498
00:25:16,681 --> 00:25:18,600
My PR is 7:28.

499
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:21,978
All right, everyone back to their warm-up.

500
00:25:22,896 --> 00:25:24,606
[rower] She's really good.

501
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:28,568
So, uh…

502
00:25:29,903 --> 00:25:32,155
What do you… What do you think?

503
00:25:32,239 --> 00:25:33,990
You should come train with us
again next week.

504
00:25:34,074 --> 00:25:36,368
We have a slot in our program.
You might be a fit.

505
00:25:36,451 --> 00:25:38,119
[Teagan laughs]

506
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,704
That sounds amazing.

507
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:42,958
Uh…

508
00:25:43,041 --> 00:25:49,047
If I go to Gravenhurst,
would I still be able to cox?

509
00:25:49,130 --> 00:25:51,967
No. We want our rowers
focused in their streams.

510
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:53,218
It's one or the other.

511
00:25:53,969 --> 00:25:56,096
-Is that a problem?
-[troubled music playing]

512
00:25:56,179 --> 00:25:57,180
No.

513
00:26:04,187 --> 00:26:06,690
Hey! Sorry I'm late.

514
00:26:07,190 --> 00:26:10,110
You're sweating. Did you already work out?

515
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:14,864
Just the jog up.
Don't worry about it. You ready?

516
00:26:14,948 --> 00:26:16,825
-Yeah. Good.
-Okay. Come on.

517
00:26:21,538 --> 00:26:22,872
[both panting]

518
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:24,457
That wasn't so bad.

519
00:26:25,041 --> 00:26:27,544
-Oh, yeah. Okay.
-Teagan!

520
00:26:28,044 --> 00:26:30,005
Jogging after an erg session.

521
00:26:30,505 --> 00:26:33,091
That's dedication.
I spoke with the head of school.

522
00:26:33,174 --> 00:26:36,136
Gravenhurst is interested
in having you transfer mid-semester,

523
00:26:36,219 --> 00:26:37,804
get you training with us right away.

524
00:26:38,513 --> 00:26:39,514
Wow.

525
00:26:40,432 --> 00:26:41,600
Uh, thank you.

526
00:26:46,354 --> 00:26:49,816
-Uh…
-A transfer to Gravenhurst Academy.

527
00:26:49,899 --> 00:26:52,319
-Crabby, I can explain--
-You tried out for them?

528
00:26:54,404 --> 00:26:56,573
Were you gonna tell us
or were you just gonna split?

529
00:26:56,656 --> 00:26:59,993
-I didn't think that far.
-I thought we were a team.

530
00:27:00,076 --> 00:27:03,580
-And now, you're just gonna cut bait?
-Well, hey, I'm a rower first.

531
00:27:03,663 --> 00:27:05,915
-I never set out to be a coxie.
-Then why did you join?

532
00:27:05,999 --> 00:27:08,001
Because it was all Easton had!

533
00:27:10,003 --> 00:27:11,546
[dramatic music playing]

534
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:13,590
You never gave a crap about us.

535
00:27:14,090 --> 00:27:16,092
You were always just in it for yourself.

536
00:27:16,176 --> 00:27:17,469
That's not true.

537
00:27:17,552 --> 00:27:21,806
You don't get to chase
your own finish line and call it teamwork.

538
00:27:22,390 --> 00:27:25,268
You should go. Don't let this deadweight
hold you back any longer.

539
00:27:25,894 --> 00:27:26,895
Crab…

540
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:37,614
[Teagan sighs]

541
00:27:38,406 --> 00:27:39,407
Hey!

542
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:41,451
-Hey.
-How was the tryout?

543
00:27:41,534 --> 00:27:42,702
Did you bomb?

544
00:27:43,203 --> 00:27:44,954
I got in.

545
00:27:45,747 --> 00:27:48,249
I thought you'd be, like, happier.

546
00:27:49,626 --> 00:27:51,503
I don't know, I'm confused.

547
00:27:54,172 --> 00:27:59,135
I just, I thought rowing
was all I ever wanted, but I…

548
00:27:59,219 --> 00:28:03,723
I don't know now.
I think I'm going to miss coxing the boys.

549
00:28:04,641 --> 00:28:07,560
Sorry, kiddo.
Sometimes you've got to choose.

550
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:09,646
["Dramamine" by Middle Kids playing]

551
00:28:12,857 --> 00:28:14,609
<i>♪ I wanna be ♪</i>

552
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:17,153
<i>-♪ I wanna be your little figurine ♪</i>
-[people cheering]

553
00:28:17,237 --> 00:28:21,241
<i>♪ You know I never meant to tell you</i>
<i>Just how much it meant to me ♪</i>

554
00:28:21,324 --> 00:28:24,953
<i>♪ And we could go around</i>
<i>Wherever you want I'll come along ♪</i>

555
00:28:25,036 --> 00:28:29,290
<i>♪ Does that sound okay to you?</i>
<i>Sometimes I wanna say to you ♪</i>

556
00:28:29,374 --> 00:28:34,796
<i>♪ You are the only reason</i>
<i>I believe in anything ♪</i>

557
00:28:34,879 --> 00:28:37,382
<i>♪ I hope you don't take this</i>
<i>The wrong way ♪</i>

558
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:42,971
<i>♪ You are the only reason</i>
<i>I believe in anything ♪</i>

559
00:28:43,054 --> 00:28:45,932
<i>♪ I hope you don't take this</i>
<i>The wrong way ♪</i>

560
00:28:46,015 --> 00:28:51,062
<i>♪ You are the only reason</i>
<i>I believe in anything ♪</i>

561
00:28:51,146 --> 00:28:54,149
<i>♪ In anything, in anything ♪</i>

562
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:59,863
<i>♪ You are the only reason</i>
<i>I believe in anything ♪</i>

563
00:29:00,363 --> 00:29:03,283
All right, Easton crew, your cox
brought you some snacks. Huddle up.

564
00:29:03,366 --> 00:29:05,452
-[rowers exclaiming]
-[Noah] Okay, Coxie!

565
00:29:05,535 --> 00:29:06,536
-Thank you.
-[Teagan] Whoa.

566
00:29:06,619 --> 00:29:08,079
[Baloo] Give me some of that.

567
00:29:08,163 --> 00:29:11,708
Oh, my gosh. You guys are human vacuums.

568
00:29:11,791 --> 00:29:14,461
-Okay, you don't need that many.
-[Hayden] Not the rinds.

569
00:29:14,544 --> 00:29:15,545
[Noah] Here, Quaid.

570
00:29:15,628 --> 00:29:17,255
-That's for you.
-[Quaid] Noah!

571
00:29:17,338 --> 00:29:18,673
-You got two?
-These are good.

572
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:31,394
Here you go.

573
00:29:31,936 --> 00:29:33,188
Can't eat right now.

574
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:37,400
You didn't tell the team about my tryout.

575
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:39,944
They have to focus for the race, so…

576
00:29:40,028 --> 00:29:41,321
Crabby.

577
00:29:41,988 --> 00:29:45,283
This isn't personal. If I leave, it'll be
because it's the right thing for me.

578
00:29:45,366 --> 00:29:47,243
-I'd want any of you to do the same.
-I know.

579
00:29:47,327 --> 00:29:48,703
It's just…

580
00:29:49,537 --> 00:29:51,206
You brought the team together.

581
00:29:51,831 --> 00:29:54,417
-Are you really going to leave us?
-You'll be fine.

582
00:29:54,501 --> 00:29:57,253
You have another cox. You have… Liam.

583
00:29:57,337 --> 00:30:00,548
[groans] You can't just swap out a cox.

584
00:30:00,632 --> 00:30:03,009
Come on. We're not a team of eight.
We're a team of nine.

585
00:30:03,092 --> 00:30:04,260
Crabby…

586
00:30:04,344 --> 00:30:05,845
You're still a rower.

587
00:30:05,929 --> 00:30:08,515
Come on. You just got
your personal best with us.

588
00:30:08,598 --> 00:30:11,142
-So just stay.
-I have to be on the water.

589
00:30:11,226 --> 00:30:14,479
It's just part of me.
Would you really hold me back from that?

590
00:30:14,562 --> 00:30:16,022
Okay, I get it.

591
00:30:16,564 --> 00:30:21,277
You know, sometimes the lead singer
has to leave the band and go solo.

592
00:30:21,778 --> 00:30:22,987
Beyoncé.

593
00:30:23,071 --> 00:30:24,405
Harry Styles.

594
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:25,365
Justin Timberlake.

595
00:30:26,574 --> 00:30:27,992
But anyway, it doesn't…

596
00:30:28,493 --> 00:30:29,994
I get it, okay?

597
00:30:30,078 --> 00:30:34,290
But I just, I wish you could, like,
just row and still cox with us.

598
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:36,584
Me too.

599
00:30:37,085 --> 00:30:38,920
But Easton doesn't have a girls' team.

600
00:30:39,003 --> 00:30:41,047
-Why not?
-They didn't have enough interest.

601
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:44,008
And they'd only consider it
if the boys started winning.

602
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:47,053
Well, why don't we just win, then?

603
00:30:47,971 --> 00:30:51,307
[suspenseful music playing]

604
00:30:52,725 --> 00:30:53,601
[Ryder laughing]

605
00:30:53,685 --> 00:30:55,311
[Teagan] Yeah. Why don't we?

606
00:30:57,105 --> 00:31:00,149
[man over PA] Bow number four.
Westvale Academy. On the paddle.

607
00:31:03,027 --> 00:31:04,445
All right, Eagles!

608
00:31:04,529 --> 00:31:09,158
Remember, we're not racing anyone.
The only boat we're racing is ourselves.

609
00:31:09,242 --> 00:31:12,620
Just us on this river,
against the clock and the pain cave.

610
00:31:12,704 --> 00:31:14,122
I'll keep the turns tight.

611
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:17,083
-Save the legs for a sprint home.
-[man] Westvale Academy.

612
00:31:17,166 --> 00:31:18,543
-Go.
-[horn blowing]

613
00:31:18,626 --> 00:31:20,837
-[people cheer]
-["Prize Fighter" by Jean Dawson playing]

614
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:22,547
[Teagan] It's our turn after Westvale.

615
00:31:22,630 --> 00:31:25,216
-You look nervous, Coxie.
-[Teagan] The bridge into that turn.

616
00:31:25,300 --> 00:31:26,676
It's a big one for me.

617
00:31:26,759 --> 00:31:27,969
You got this?

618
00:31:29,304 --> 00:31:30,346
We'll find out.

619
00:31:31,264 --> 00:31:32,724
All right, we're up.

620
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:35,101
Bow number 5.

621
00:31:35,643 --> 00:31:38,187
Easton Prep. On the paddle.

622
00:31:38,271 --> 00:31:40,273
[people cheering]

623
00:31:40,356 --> 00:31:43,902
<i>♪ I'll be in my way</i>
<i>When no one's watching ♪</i>

624
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:47,322
-Easton Prep, go!
-[horn blows]

625
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:49,407
[people cheering]

626
00:31:52,118 --> 00:31:54,120
<i>♪ I go all the way ♪</i>

627
00:31:59,334 --> 00:32:04,130
<i>♪ I go all… ♪</i>

628
00:32:04,213 --> 00:32:06,758
All right, port! Pressure!

629
00:32:06,841 --> 00:32:09,135
Bridge ahead. Line it up!

630
00:32:09,969 --> 00:32:15,266
Ryder, set us up for the bridge.
Safely. Stay low!

631
00:32:18,770 --> 00:32:20,188
[Ryder] Starboard!

632
00:32:20,813 --> 00:32:23,399
Too much! Starboard!

633
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:28,780
Let up! Let me steer!

634
00:32:30,823 --> 00:32:32,867
Stay even.

635
00:32:33,660 --> 00:32:38,790
Okay! Okay, Eagles,
that's a good run! Here we go!

636
00:32:38,873 --> 00:32:42,085
Port pressure! Turn! Turn!

637
00:32:42,168 --> 00:32:44,796
All right! And we're through.

638
00:32:49,008 --> 00:32:51,010
<i>♪ I go all the way ♪</i>

639
00:32:56,849 --> 00:32:59,394
Last thousand meters. Hold on!

640
00:33:04,857 --> 00:33:07,777
Breathe! Keep it in your fingers.

641
00:33:08,903 --> 00:33:09,821
[grunts]

642
00:33:15,576 --> 00:33:17,495
Hey guys, there's Westvale!

643
00:33:17,578 --> 00:33:20,623
We don't have to beat them to win.
Just stay on their tail.

644
00:33:20,707 --> 00:33:22,542
Crabby, come on!

645
00:33:22,625 --> 00:33:25,420
Take that exit!
We need to power through, okay?

646
00:33:25,503 --> 00:33:29,632
Guys, let's end this race together!
Who are you pulling for?

647
00:33:29,716 --> 00:33:34,053
The engine room that never quits.
Tried and true, our Baloo!

648
00:33:34,137 --> 00:33:35,888
-Yes, yeah!
-For Ryder!

649
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:37,932
-[rowers] Yeah!
-[Teagan] For Cam!

650
00:33:38,016 --> 00:33:39,934
-Yeah!
-For Josh!

651
00:33:40,018 --> 00:33:42,103
For Quaid!

652
00:33:42,186 --> 00:33:43,604
-For Noah!
-Yeah!

653
00:33:44,230 --> 00:33:45,606
-For Perry!
-Yeah!

654
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:50,069
For the heart and soul of our team,
for Crabcatcher!

655
00:33:50,987 --> 00:33:54,532
Now, send it!

656
00:33:54,615 --> 00:33:56,075
[Ryder] Go! Go!

657
00:33:56,159 --> 00:33:57,035
Four…

658
00:33:57,660 --> 00:33:59,078
Three, come on!

659
00:33:59,162 --> 00:34:00,955
Two…

660
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:03,875
One, and we're out!

661
00:34:03,958 --> 00:34:07,795
[people cheering]

662
00:34:13,217 --> 00:34:14,761
[Teagan] Nice work, guys.

663
00:34:15,344 --> 00:34:16,471
Let's see if it's enough.

664
00:34:16,554 --> 00:34:18,598
[rowers panting]

665
00:34:21,934 --> 00:34:23,311
[tense music playing]

666
00:34:23,394 --> 00:34:25,229
Waiting for the final times.

667
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:36,532
-Oh my God.
-What?

668
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:39,702
-We won!
-Yeah!

669
00:34:41,412 --> 00:34:43,122
Let's go!

670
00:34:43,206 --> 00:34:45,208
[all screaming and cheering]

671
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:47,752
[Noah] Yeah!

672
00:34:49,754 --> 00:34:51,589
Good job, Stroke!

673
00:34:52,423 --> 00:34:54,967
[Teagan whooping]

674
00:35:00,556 --> 00:35:01,557
-Nice race.
-Ace.

675
00:35:01,641 --> 00:35:03,059
-Nice job.
-Nice race.

676
00:35:03,142 --> 00:35:04,393
-Good race.
-Nice race.

677
00:35:04,477 --> 00:35:05,561
Nice race.

678
00:35:06,729 --> 00:35:07,939
[Hayden] Way to go, Coxie!

679
00:35:08,689 --> 00:35:09,690
Good job.

680
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:11,484
Good job!

681
00:35:12,860 --> 00:35:13,945
Good race.

682
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:15,321
[Hayden] Good job!

683
00:35:16,989 --> 00:35:17,990
Coach.

684
00:35:18,491 --> 00:35:19,450
[Hayden] Big man.

685
00:35:19,534 --> 00:35:21,369
-[laughing]
-Yeah.

686
00:35:24,997 --> 00:35:27,500
Crew. This is your moment.

687
00:35:28,251 --> 00:35:29,252
Take it all in.

688
00:35:29,335 --> 00:35:31,587
[team cheering]

689
00:35:33,923 --> 00:35:35,967
Let's go!

690
00:35:37,677 --> 00:35:40,012
-Eagle pride!
-[team] Eagle pride!

691
00:35:40,096 --> 00:35:41,931
Eagle pride!

692
00:35:44,892 --> 00:35:47,270
-Eagle pride!
-Come on.

693
00:35:47,937 --> 00:35:49,730
-[Baloo] Crabby!
-[rower] Crabby!

694
00:35:49,814 --> 00:35:52,692
-Go, Crabby!
-[rower] <i>♪ Olé, olé, olé, olé ♪</i>

695
00:35:53,568 --> 00:35:55,319
Whoo!

696
00:35:55,903 --> 00:35:56,737
[Baloo] Oh, yeah!

697
00:36:01,909 --> 00:36:02,994
[Perry] Whoo!

698
00:36:03,077 --> 00:36:04,579
Hey, we did it, man.

699
00:36:04,662 --> 00:36:07,623
Yeah, you know,
just a guy who phones it in.

700
00:36:07,707 --> 00:36:09,000
Stumbles into gold.

701
00:36:09,667 --> 00:36:11,836
Yeah. Yeah, I heard
what you said about me.

702
00:36:13,254 --> 00:36:14,255
Bro.

703
00:36:15,131 --> 00:36:16,632
You know what I meant. It's…

704
00:36:17,133 --> 00:36:21,596
We know you try hard. It's just,
we'd kill to be in the engine room.

705
00:36:22,138 --> 00:36:23,264
Oh.

706
00:36:23,347 --> 00:36:25,308
So you're jealous of me. Yeah.

707
00:36:25,391 --> 00:36:27,143
-All right.
-Okay. Slow your roll.

708
00:36:29,061 --> 00:36:33,399
[laughing] So, you staying?

709
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:35,193
We won.

710
00:36:35,276 --> 00:36:37,737
Next up, girls' team.

711
00:36:37,820 --> 00:36:39,030
We're doing it all.

712
00:36:39,113 --> 00:36:40,364
[both laughing]

713
00:36:41,449 --> 00:36:42,992
Oh, Crabby.

714
00:36:43,075 --> 00:36:47,705
But there is one tradition
being a rower will not get you out of.

715
00:36:47,788 --> 00:36:49,790
[whistles sharply] Hey, guys.

716
00:36:49,874 --> 00:36:53,419
Someone is a little dry.

717
00:36:53,502 --> 00:36:55,755
-Oh no! No, don't you dare!
-[team clamoring]

718
00:36:55,838 --> 00:36:59,258
No, don't you dare! Crabby! No!

719
00:36:59,342 --> 00:37:00,718
To the water!

720
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:03,804
["Heartthrob" by Indigo De Souza playing]

721
00:37:03,888 --> 00:37:06,807
<i>♪ I really put my back into it ♪</i>

722
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:09,560
<i>♪ I really put my back into it ♪</i>

723
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:12,021
[Teagan screaming]

724
00:37:19,528 --> 00:37:24,700
[team cheering]

725
00:37:24,784 --> 00:37:26,369
Party in my room!

726
00:37:26,452 --> 00:37:28,287
[team] Yeah!

727
00:37:28,371 --> 00:37:30,498
[Quaid] Party, party, party!

728
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:33,000
[Teagan] Do you see
what I've been putting up with?

729
00:37:33,084 --> 00:37:34,835
[Ella] Yes, I can see.

730
00:37:34,919 --> 00:37:36,295
[Crabcatcher] Hey, you coming?

731
00:37:36,796 --> 00:37:38,589
-We have dinner, so…
-No, no, no, no!

732
00:37:38,673 --> 00:37:40,466
You gotta go. Come on.

733
00:37:41,008 --> 00:37:42,885
Go celebrate with the boys. [laughs]

734
00:37:42,969 --> 00:37:43,970
[phone buzzes]

735
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:47,139
Um, it's my dad. Meet you in there?

736
00:37:47,223 --> 00:37:48,307
Yeah.

737
00:37:48,391 --> 00:37:49,392
Cool.

738
00:37:53,646 --> 00:37:54,480
Uh, hello?

739
00:37:54,563 --> 00:37:56,440
You're a hard man
to get a hold of, Mr. Regis.

740
00:37:57,358 --> 00:37:59,318
Sorry, Dr. Monroe, I've been busy.

741
00:37:59,402 --> 00:38:01,112
I'm calling to see
why you haven't scheduled

742
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:02,905
the follow-up test I recommended.

743
00:38:03,447 --> 00:38:06,909
I'm feeling good. Yeah, the beta blockers
you prescribed are working.

744
00:38:06,993 --> 00:38:08,869
<i>Those were just a temporary solution.</i>

745
00:38:08,953 --> 00:38:12,248
Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy
is a serious condition, Josh.

746
00:38:12,331 --> 00:38:13,165
Right.

747
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:15,167
<i>We need to monitor your heart to ensure</i>

748
00:38:15,251 --> 00:38:17,211
the left ventricle
hasn't thickened further.

749
00:38:17,295 --> 00:38:18,129
If it does…

750
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:20,756
Dr. Monroe,
I've been feeling fine. Really.

751
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:24,010
<i>The state allows physicians</i>
<i>to treat minors on their own.</i>

752
00:38:24,093 --> 00:38:28,180
But if you don't take treatment seriously,
I'll have to involve your parents.

753
00:38:28,264 --> 00:38:30,933
No need to do that.
I'll schedule the test right away.

754
00:38:37,356 --> 00:38:39,317
Let there be two!

755
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:40,985
-To Easton Crew!
-[Quaid] Drink it!

756
00:38:41,068 --> 00:38:43,195
-Yes!
-[Perry] Bottom's up, boys!

757
00:38:43,696 --> 00:38:46,324
-[Ryder] Let's go. More.
-Pers, drink up, there's more.

758
00:38:46,407 --> 00:38:48,159
What a big win!

759
00:38:48,659 --> 00:38:50,578
And a double congratulations, I think.

760
00:38:50,661 --> 00:38:52,705
I heard you got your spot
with Gravenhurst.

761
00:38:52,788 --> 00:38:53,831
Ha…

762
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:56,625
I appreciate the offer.

763
00:38:56,709 --> 00:38:58,127
Of course.

764
00:38:58,711 --> 00:39:00,338
But I decided not to go.

765
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:03,049
Wow.

766
00:39:03,132 --> 00:39:04,925
Yeah. Uh…

767
00:39:05,676 --> 00:39:07,219
[Teagan laughing]

768
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:10,056
My team is my team.

769
00:39:10,681 --> 00:39:12,099
You'll regret this.

770
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:14,602
Yo. Apologies.

771
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:17,480
We need our coxie
to report to the starting line.

772
00:39:18,022 --> 00:39:20,483
-Jell-O shots!
-[Teagan] Okay!

773
00:39:21,650 --> 00:39:22,693
Crabby!

774
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:24,403
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

775
00:39:24,904 --> 00:39:26,030
What are you doing over here?

776
00:39:26,113 --> 00:39:29,033
-I thought you'd be talking to Teagan.
-I'm going to.

777
00:39:30,618 --> 00:39:31,619
Okay.

778
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:35,998
For some reason, every time I talk to her,
something goes horribly wrong.

779
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:37,416
So I'm just gonna take a minute.

780
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:39,585
[Madison] She's a complex case, isn't she?

781
00:39:39,668 --> 00:39:41,379
[Cam] I don't wanna screw this up.

782
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:44,006
Why can't she be easy to talk to like you?

783
00:39:48,177 --> 00:39:49,303
[Quaid laughing]

784
00:39:49,929 --> 00:39:51,430
-[Teagan laughs]
-[Quaid] Ahh!

785
00:39:52,014 --> 00:39:52,973
Okay.

786
00:39:53,557 --> 00:39:54,725
I'm gonna do it.

787
00:39:59,647 --> 00:40:02,775
Hey, Teagan. I hope this comes out right.

788
00:40:02,858 --> 00:40:06,529
I wasn't sure about earlier.
Um, I'd like to take you out.

789
00:40:06,612 --> 00:40:09,198
-And I don't know why this is so hard…
-Yes.

790
00:40:09,281 --> 00:40:10,157
Tacos.

791
00:40:10,241 --> 00:40:12,368
-Okay. Tacos.
-[laughing]

792
00:40:13,119 --> 00:40:14,620
[knocking]

793
00:40:17,915 --> 00:40:19,375
[sighs]

794
00:40:27,007 --> 00:40:28,134
Hmm.

795
00:40:28,926 --> 00:40:31,262
Steak and cake for one.

796
00:40:38,519 --> 00:40:40,521
[phone line ringing]

797
00:40:41,313 --> 00:40:43,566
<i>Hey, it's David. Leave a message.</i>

798
00:40:43,649 --> 00:40:44,775
[beeps]

799
00:40:45,609 --> 00:40:46,819
Hi.

800
00:40:48,571 --> 00:40:50,364
I don't know if you'll get this.

801
00:40:51,157 --> 00:40:53,993
You were always better
at remembering our anniversary than I was.

802
00:40:54,076 --> 00:40:56,078
[somber music playing]

803
00:40:57,204 --> 00:41:01,250
I'm sitting in this beautiful room,
with a beautiful meal,

804
00:41:01,750 --> 00:41:04,920
after watching our beautiful girl
win gold,

805
00:41:05,004 --> 00:41:08,424
and all I can think about is
where the hell are you?

806
00:41:12,052 --> 00:41:14,680
You know,
I still sleep on the left side of the bed

807
00:41:14,763 --> 00:41:19,185
because after 18 years,
some habits are hard to break, but…

808
00:41:20,811 --> 00:41:22,730
you don't get to haunt me anymore.

809
00:41:25,483 --> 00:41:26,484
I'm done.

810
00:41:31,030 --> 00:41:33,032
[expectant music playing]

811
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:38,579
[knocking]

812
00:41:43,375 --> 00:41:44,919
-Hey.
-Hi.

813
00:41:45,002 --> 00:41:48,255
Do you wanna… go to the bar
and get a drink?

814
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:51,091
Yeah. Yeah.

815
00:41:54,929 --> 00:41:56,931
[muffled chatter behind door]

816
00:41:57,765 --> 00:41:58,807
[sighs]

817
00:42:04,897 --> 00:42:05,731
[exhales]

818
00:42:07,525 --> 00:42:08,776
[Teagan laughing] Wow! Okay.

819
00:42:08,859 --> 00:42:12,821
[team chanting] Drink! Drink! Drink!

820
00:42:12,905 --> 00:42:14,448
-Drink!
-[Quaid] Yeah!

821
00:42:15,241 --> 00:42:16,325
Bro, you made it!

822
00:42:16,825 --> 00:42:18,577
Hell yeah, bro. I wouldn't miss it.

823
00:42:19,537 --> 00:42:22,540
-Josh Regis.
-Teagan Tao.

824
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:26,752
I believe it's your turn with the cup.

825
00:42:30,047 --> 00:42:31,924
I don't wanna be just friends.

826
00:42:32,007 --> 00:42:33,300
[stirring music playing]

827
00:42:33,384 --> 00:42:40,099
-[team chanting] Easton! Easton! Easton!
-[Perry] Josh!

828
00:42:40,599 --> 00:42:47,064
[chanting continues]

829
00:42:48,857 --> 00:42:50,859
[music continues]

830
00:43:45,873 --> 00:43:47,833
[music ends]
